Backport of SoftHSMv2 PR #857 (main f59e8f47fbdc, "Support multipart operation on hashed ECDSA",
merged 2026-07-09, after 2.7.0) to 2.7.0, OpenSSL backend only.

2.7.0 lists CKM_ECDSA_SHA1..SHA512 but allows them single-part only: C_SignUpdate returns
CKR_OPERATION_NOT_INITIALIZED, so a streaming caller (OpenSSL's `dgst -sign` through
pkcs11-provider) cannot sign. Changes from upstream: the OSSLECDSA init signatures take
2.7.0's (param, paramLen) instead of main's MechanismParam (#833), and the Botan backend's hunks
are left out (nixpkgs builds the OpenSSL one). Drop with a SoftHSM release that carries #857.

